    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Fellow-in-AI-and-Multimedia-Security-%28HG%29/1173-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in AI and Multimedia Security (HG) Job Details",
      "description": "Research Fellow in AI and Multimedia Security (HG) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Fellow in AI and Multimedia Security (HG) Posting Start Date: 09/10/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Networks & Cybersecurity Employment Type: Fixed Term About the Job The Infocomm Technology (ICT) Cluster at the Singapore Institute of Technology invites applications for a Research Fellow on a 1-year contract under an AI Singapore-funded research programme on copyright protection for AI-assisted creative content. The programme develops technical safeguards that make visual content, including video and animation, verifiable, traceable, and revocable in AI-assisted production workflows. Responsibilities: 1. Conduct research on robust watermarking for deep learning models and AI-generated visual content, including video and other temporal media. 2. Publish research findings in top-tier conferences and journals, and present research outcomes. 3. Maintain and update research documentation, code, and the Python programming platform. 4. Contribute to project deliverables and reports, and collaborate with project partners. 5. Assist with project-related student training. 6. Assist with project-related administrative matters. Requirements: 1. A PhD in computer science, electrical engineering, or related fields. 2. Research experience in deep learning model watermarking, media watermarking, or AI security. 3. Proficient in Python machine learning libraries, especially PyTorch. 4. Strong technical paper writing skills, with submission and publication in the above areas. 5. Self-motivated, able to deliver results within a fixed timeframe, and good at communication and presentation. 6. Experience in video watermarking or watermarking for other temporal visual media will be an advantage. 7. Experience in model watermarking, watermark removal attacks, or model extraction will be an advantage. 8. Familiarity with machine unlearning or concept erasure in generative models will be an advantage. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from pr