    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Fellow-Research-Engineer-%28AI-and-Data-Analytics-for-Food-and-Nutrition-Systems%29-MM3/1172-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI and Data Analytics for Food and Nutrition Systems)",
      "description": "Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI and Data Analytics for Food and Nutrition Systems) - MM3 Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI and Data Analytics for Food and Nutrition Systems) - MM3 Posting Start Date: 09/10/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Food, Chemical and Biotechnology Employment Type: Fixed Term As a University of Applied Learning, SIT works closely with industry in our research pursuits. Our research staff will have the opportunity to be equipped with applied research skill sets that are relevant to industry demands while working on research projects in SIT. The Research Fellow / Research Engineer will support a research project focused on the development of data-driven modelling, optimisation, and decision-support tools for food and nutrition systems. The successful candidate will work closely with the Principal Investigator on research activities involving data analytics, computational modelling, machine learning, and optimisation. The role offers opportunities to contribute to research publications, technical development, and industry-relevant project outcomes in the areas of food sustainability, nutrition, and supply chain decision-making. Key Responsibilities Support the research project to ensure milestones and deliverables are achieved. Collect, organise, process, and analyse datasets from various sources. Develop computational models, data analytics workflows, and decision-support tools. Conduct data analysis, visualisation, model validation, and performance evaluation. Assist in the development and testing of machine learning and optimisation models. Support the integration and analysis of food, nutrition, sustainability, and related datasets. Prepare technical reports, research documentation, presentations, journal publications, and conference materials. Support student projects and other research activities related to the project. Assist in project coordination, progress reporting, and research administration. Follow SIT requirements on data management, research integrity, intellectual property, cybersecurity, and workplace safety. Communicate with relevant internal or external stakeholders to support project activities and deliverables. Any ad-hoc duties assigned by the Supervisor. Job Requirements Bachelor ’ s or Master’s degree degree in Engineering, Computer Science, Data Science, Applied Mathematics, Statistics, Operations Research, Industrial Engineering, Food Science, Nutrition, or a related discipline. Applicants with a PhD may be considered for appointment as Research Fellow. Interest or experience in food systems, nutrition, sustainability, supply chains, or related application domains is advantageous. Good programming skills in Python or other relevant programming languages. Experience in data analysis, modelling, machine learning, optimisation, software development, or scientific computing is advantageous. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and quantitative skills. Ability to learn new methods and tools independently. Good written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a research environment. Strong organisational skills and ability to manage multiple tasks and meet project deadlines. Key Competencies Proficient in Python or equivalent programming languages for data analysis and modelling. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and quantitative skills. Ability to develop and validate computational models and data-driven solutions. Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare technical reports and presentations. Self-motivated, able to work independently, and committed to continuous learning. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely 