    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-EngineerFellow-%285G-Software-Solution%29-PY/1169-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Engineer/Fellow (5G Software Solution)",
      "description": "Research Engineer/Fellow (5G Software Solution) - PY Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Engineer/Fellow (5G Software Solution) - PY Posting Start Date: 05/10/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Networks & Cybersecurity Employment Type: Fixed Term Job Purpose The Future Communications Translation Lab (FCTLab) at the Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT) is seeking a motivated candidate who is keen on both rigorous research and the practical application of 5G and future communication technologies. As part of the research team, you will collaborate with faculty and industry partners to drive innovation in 5G/6G technologies and their real-world use cases. Equipped with private 5G testbeds and advanced test and measurement instruments, FCTLab provides an ideal environment to develop, validate, and refine next-generation communication technologies while accelerating their translation into impactful and industry-ready solutions. As a Software Solution Engineer, you will design, develop and integrate software solutions and working prototypes that translate FCTLab’s research into practical applications, supporting the demonstration and validation of 5G-enabled use cases with industry partners. Key Responsibilities Work with researchers and industry partners to understand use-case requirements, assess technical feasibility, and propose system architectures, software designs and suitable hardware components. Develop proof-of-concept applications and working prototypes through hands-on software development, translating research outcomes into practical solutions. Integrate software with devices, cameras, sensors, actuators and communication interfaces. Incorporate AI models, video processing and streaming capabilities where relevant to project needs. Design and conduct functional and performance tests, troubleshoot integration issues, and refine prototypes to support laboratory experiments, field trials and demonstrations. Work closely with the Principal Investigator, Co-PI and research team to plan development activities and deliver project milestones. Where development is outsourced, define technical requirements, coordinate with vendors and verify deliverable quality. Prepare software documentation, technical reports and demonstration materials. Contribute to feasibility studies, collaboration proposals and publications where relevant. Maintain prototype software and development environments, and provide technical guidance to students and researchers on software development, integration and testing. Job Requirements At least 6 years of relevant experience in software development and system design, with hands-on experience in developing working prototypes or integrated applications. At least Bachelor’s, master's or Ph.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Computer Science or a related field. Strong software design and programming skills in Python and C++, with the ability to translate use-case requirements into maintainable software. Good understanding of wireless communications and networking, particularly 5G/LTE and Wi-Fi, with the ability to relate their capabilities and limitations to application requirements and translate the lab’s research into practical prototypes that demonstrate the value of these technologies. Hands-on experience in hardware–software integration, including interfacing with  sensors, actuators, modems or cameras and software components through REST APIs, messaging systems, Websocket etc. Good understanding of computer networking fundamentals such as TCP/UDP/IP, sockets, VPN, NAT and tunneling as well as connectivity technologies such as MPTCP, Wireguard or MPQUIC. Hands-on experience with Linux networking utilities tools like iperf, iproute2, nmcli, tcpdump and wireshark etc. Knowledge or experience in video processing and streaming is highly preferred, including video capture, encoding/decoding, real-time processing or low-latency transmission. Knowledge or experience in AI, machine learning and computer vision is highly preferred, particularly in integrating AI models into practical applications. Experience with ROS/ROS 2, embedded systems, real-time operating systems or deployment on edge computing platforms is an advantage. Strong analytical, technical and problem-solving skills. Strong communication and technical writing skills. Self-motivated, team-oriented and able to work independently with minimal supervision. Key Competencies Able to build and maintain strong working relationships with people within and external to the university. Self-directed learner who believes in continuous learning and development Proficient in technical writing and presentation Possess strong analytical and critical thinking skills Show strong initiative and take ownership of work Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of