    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Engineer-%28Embodied-AI-Systems-Integration-Engineer%29-EA10/1165-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (Embodied AI Systems Integration Engineer)",
      "description": "Research Engineer (Embodied AI Systems Integration Engineer) - EA10 Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Research Engineer (Embodied AI Systems Integration Engineer) - EA10 We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Engineer (Embodied AI Systems Integration Engineer) - EA10 Posting Start Date: 29/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Mechanical & Systems Engineering Employment Type: Fixed Term Embodied AI Systems Integration Engineer / Research Engineer Job Purpose As a University of Applied Learning, SIT works closely with industry and research partners in our research pursuits. The primary responsibility of this role is to support the project management, coordination and technical integration of a research project developing embodied AI and robotic systems for aircraft cargo loading operations. The Research Engineer will coordinate project activities across research teams, industry partners and vendors, while also supporting system integration, testing and deployment of robotic, perception, simulation and AI components. Key Responsibilities Support the PI/Co-PIs in project planning, coordination, tracking of milestones and deliverables, and preparation of project reviews and reports. Coordinate activities across research work packages, industry partners, vendors and other stakeholders. Manage project schedules, technical documentation, procurement, equipment delivery, testing activities and follow-up actions. Support integration of robotic systems including manipulators, mobile robots, perception systems, sensors and control software. Support development and testing of embodied AI workflows including teleoperation, simulation, data collection and learning-based robotic policies. Coordinate and conduct system integration, experimental testing and validation in laboratory and representative aircraft cargo environments. Troubleshoot technical integration issues and work with relevant teams to ensure project deliverables are achieved. Prepare technical reports, presentation materials, meeting records and project documentation. Support Risk Assessment, Workplace Safety and Health requirements, equipment maintenance and student project supervision. Job Requirements Bachelor’s, Master’s or PhD degree in Robotics, Mechanical/Mechatronics Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science or related fields. Experience in project coordination or management of engineering/research projects. Good understanding of robotics systems integration, preferably involving ROS/ROS2, robotic manipulators, mobile robots or perception systems. Familiarity with robotics simulation platforms such as NVIDIA Isaac Sim, Isaac Lab, Gazebo or MuJoCo. Strong organisational, communication and stakeholder-management skills. Able to work independently and coordinate multidisciplinary technical teams. Experience with embodied AI, teleoperation, robotic manipulation, perception or sim-to-real workflows will be advantageous. Key Competencies Strong project coordination and organisational skills. Good systems-level understanding of robotics and embodied AI. Strong communication and stakeholder-management skills. Hands-on, proactive and able to resolve technical and coordination issues. Able to manage multiple workstreams, timelines and deliverables concurrently. Major Challenges Coordinating multiple research teams, industry partners and technical work packages. Managing project timelines while resolving cross-system integration dependencies. Integrating robotics, perception, simulation and AI components into a reliable end-to-end demonstrator. Balancing research development with project delivery, safety and operational requirements. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note th