    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Fellow-Engineer-%28Project-Manager-Biodiversity%29-JK4/1137-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Fellow / Engineer (Project Manager-Biodiversity)",
      "description": "Research Fellow / Engineer (Project Manager-Biodiversity) - JK4 Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Fellow / Engineer (Project Manager-Biodiversity) - JK4 Posting Start Date: 24/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Engineering Employment Type: Fixed Term Job Purpose As a University of Applied Learning, SIT works closely with industry or government agencies in our research pursuits. Our research staff will have the opportunity to be equipped with applied research skill sets that are relevant to industry demands while working on research projects in SIT. The primary responsibility of this role is to deliver on an industry innovation research project where you will be help the PI manage and be involved in multiple research teams to develop/produce/investigate coastal biodiversity and environmental sustainability related projects (with a focus on mangrove ecosystems) in the Engineering Cluster, SIT. Key Responsibilities Work with the PI as a project manager to supervise and manage mulitple research projects to ensure all project deliverables are achieved. Undertake these responsibilites in the project Develop and organise educational and outreach programs on mangrove ecology and restoration. Involved in field studies in coastal marine habitats involving mangroves, fishes, macroinvertebrates and potentially plankton sampling Assist in laboratory-based work involving sorting and processing of specimens and data collected during field work Invovled in data analyses and technical report/scientific paper writing Co-supervise student projects with the PI. Complete, maintain and update Laboratory/Project related Risk Assessments and ensure compliance to Work, Safety and Health Regulations (WSH). Communicate effectively with any internal or external stakeholders to ensure project deliverables are met. Any other ad-hoc duties assigned by the PI. Job Requirements PhD or MSc with 6-8 years of relevant experience; prior experience in coastal ecology preferred Key Competencies Good organizational skills and excellent attention to detail is essential Possess leadership qualities, highly-motivated, responsible, and a fast learner Ability to problem solve issues independently. Independent, but also able to work well with others in a highly collaborative, team-oriented environment Proficiency in Microsoft Office and Adobe applications Experience in data analysis (using R, Primer, PC-Ord) is desirable, but training will be provided if necessary Show strong initiative and take ownership of work Major Challenges May require some level of physical fitness for extended periods of field work in tropical coastal environments Some weekend flexibility may be required Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site 