    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Senior-Manager-Assistant-Director-%28Enterprise-Risk-Management%29/1163-en_GB": {
      "title": "Senior Manager/ Assistant Director (Enterprise Risk Management) Job Details",
      "description": "Senior Manager/ Assistant Director (Enterprise Risk Management) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Senior Manager/ Assistant Director (Enterprise Risk Management) Posting Start Date: 24/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Planning, Risk and Safety Employment Type: Fixed Term We are seeking an experienced enterprise risk management professional to lead and strengthen the University’s Enterprise Risk Management programme. In this role, you will work closely with senior management and stakeholders across the University to enhance institutional resilience, promote risk-informed decision-making, and embed effective risk management practices into strategic and operational processes. You will also provide clear and actionable risk insights to support management and governance committees. Key Responsibilities Lead the development and continuous enhancement of the University’s Enterprise Risk Management framework, policies, methodologies, tools, templates, risk taxonomy, rating criteria and reporting standards. Drive the enterprise risk review cycle, including the maintenance of risk registers, risk appetite statements, key risk indicators, dashboards and management reports. Monitor internal and external developments to identify emerging risks, evolving threats and cross-cutting vulnerabilities that may affect the University. Assess risks associated with new programmes, initiatives, third-party engagements and key institutional processes, and recommend appropriate controls and mitigation measures. Analyse operational risk incidents and significant events to identify root causes, systemic themes and opportunities to strengthen organisational controls and resilience. Synthesise complex information into clear risk insights, assessments and recommendations for senior management and governance forums. Partner academic and corporate stakeholders to facilitate risk discussions, support mitigation planning and strengthen ownership and accountability for risks. Design and deliver briefings, workshops and capability-building initiatives to enhance risk literacy and promote a positive risk culture across the University. Support engagements with auditors, consultants, government agencies and governance bodies on matters relating to risk, assurance, resilience and compliance. Contribute to the integration of Enterprise Risk Management with business continuity, crisis preparedness, compliance, internal controls, strategic planning and performance monitoring. Lead or support secretariat responsibilities for key management committees, including agenda planning, review of meeting materials, preparation of briefing points and oversight of meeting records. Direct the planning and delivery of selected high-profile University events, and ensure appropriate follow-through on agreed outcomes and actions. Provide leadership and guidance to project teams, and mentor junior colleagues where required. Job Requirements A recognised university degree. At least 8 to 10 years of relevant experience in enterprise risk management or a related field, preferably within higher education, the public sector or a complex matrix organisation. A postgraduate qualification or professional certification in risk management, internal audit, business continuity, governance or a related discipline would be advantageous. Strong knowledge of Enterprise Risk Management frameworks, risk appetite, key risk indicators, risk registers, mitigation planning, assurance processes and management reporting. Strong analytical skills, with the ability to interpret complex information and translate it into clear, practical and actionable recommendations. Excellent writing, presentation, facilitation, stakeholder engagement and project leadership capabilities. Demonstrated ability to engage and work effectively with senior management and diverse stakeholders. High standards of integrity, discretion and professionalism when handling sensitive institutional information. An awareness of regional and global developments that may affect higher education, technology, partnerships, sustainability, safety, cybersecurity and institutional resilience would be valuable. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
