    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Assessment-Specialist-%28Senior-Manager-Manager%29/846-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assessment Specialist (Senior Manager / Manager) Job Details",
      "description": "Assessment Specialist (Senior Manager / Manager) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Assessment Specialist (Senior Manager / Manager) Posting Start Date: 18/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: SIT Teaching and Learning Academy Employment Type: Fixed Term The Centralised Skills Assessment and Validation Initiative (CSAVI) is a national initiative led by SIT to strengthen skills-based assessment and workforce mobility. CSAVI supports the development, validation, and scaling of robust assessment tools that enable fair, transparent, and industry-relevant skills recognition. We are looking for a detail-oriented and research-driven Assessment Specialist to lead the design, validation, and continuous improvement of our assessment tools. This role is integral to ensuring CSAVI’s assessments are fair, reliable, and evidence-based, and meet national and international standards of rigour. Key Responsibilities: Design competency-based assessment frameworks and instruments for various industry sectors and job roles. Lead the development and validation of assessment content (e.g., situational judgement tests, oral interactive assessments, simulations). Apply psychometric models to evaluate item and test performance, ensuring validity, reliability, and fairness. Conduct statistical analysis referencing appropriate theories (e.g., Classical Test Theory (CTT), Item Response Theory (IRT), and Generalisability Theory). Develop scoring rubrics, standard setting protocols, and examiner calibration tools. Analyse assessment data and generate technical reports for internal stakeholders, industry partners, and policy makers. Lead or support research studies on assessment innovations, test design, and psychometric methodologies. Ensure quality assurance in assessment delivery and advise on improvements based on analytics and international best practices. Support CSAVI leadership in end-to-end skills assessment life cycle processes to iteratively improve and optimise in-house processes. Requirements: A recognised qualification in psychometrics, instructional design, educational measurement, applied statistics, psychology, or a related field. 3–7 years of experience in assessment development, test validation, or educational measurement, preferably within higher education, CET, or licensure/certification contexts. Strong statistical and psychometric expertise, with proficiency in tools such as R, Winsteps, SPSS, or similar. Familiarity with digital assessment platforms, test security, and large-scale assessment deployment. Demonstrated ability to translate complex data into actionable insights and communicate findings to non-technical stakeholders. Experience working with diverse teams, including subject matter experts, educators, and technology partners. What We Offer: A rare opportunity to shape national-level assessment practices and psychometric standards. A collaborative work environment that blends education, innovation, and applied research. Professional development opportunities within SIT’s applied learning ecosystem. Competitive remuneration commensurate with experience and qualifications. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is