    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/IT-Consultant-%28SAP-S4-Hana-Finance%29-%2811-months-contract%29/1161-en_GB": {
      "title": "IT Consultant (SAP S/4 Hana Finance) (11-months contract) Job Details",
      "description": "IT Consultant (SAP S/4 Hana Finance) (11-months contract) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology IT Consultant (SAP S/4 Hana Finance) (11-months contract) We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now IT Consultant (SAP S/4 Hana Finance) (11-months contract) Posting Start Date: 17/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Communications & Information Technology Employment Type: Temporary Key Responsibilities Support SAP S/4 HANA Finance modules and handle incidents, service requests, and change requests independently. Provide basic support for SAP Analytics Cloud (SAC), including user enquiries, access issues, data validation, and coordination with vendors where required. Conduct user requirement analysis for enhancements, analyse business information needs, translate requirements into functional specifications, and secure user signoffs. Perform systems and data analysis, including reviewing existing system or program logic and recommending changes to improve processes where necessary. Analyse and propose data integration specifications for data exchanges with other IT systems inside and outside the organization. Evaluate potential solutions and make recommendations to business users, taking into consideration S/4HANA best practices and process standardisation. Support interfaces between non-ERP systems and SAP S/4 HANA. Liaise closely with business users, vendors, and team members to build good rapport and ensure timely resolution of support matters. Support application maintenance, user testing, patches, upgrades, and project implementation activities in accordance with established methodologies and policies. Plan, coordinate, conduct, and document end-to-end unit testing and System Integration Testing, and support users during User Acceptance Testing. Keep abreast of relevant digital tools, including Microsoft Copilot and other AI-enabled productivity solutions, and explore practical use cases to improve support efficiency. Job Requirements Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related discipline. At least 5 years of experience in an SAP Finance functional role, including systems design, configuration, functional support, and user support experience. Good working knowledge of SAP S/4 HANA Finance, including key finance processes such as General Ledger, Accounts Receivable, Accounts Payable, Asset Accounting, Bank Management, Project System, and integration with Materials Management. Hands-on experience supporting SAP S/4 HANA Finance incidents, service requests, change requests, testing, and enhancements. Basic knowledge of SAP Analytics Cloud (SAC), including dashboard/report support, data validation, access troubleshooting, and coordination with business users or vendors. Experience in working with interfaces between SAP and third-party systems. Knowledge and experience with Robotic Process Automation (RPA), data analysis tools, Vendor Invoice Management, or e-invoicing solutions will be an added advantage. Basic awareness of AI-enabled productivity tools such as Microsoft Copilot, with the ability to identify practical use cases for improving documentation, analysis, and user support. Knowledge of OData Services, SAP Business Technology Platform services, CDS views, and SAP Fiori applications would be an added advantage. Able to work independently and as an excellent team player. Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills, with the ability to understand functional requirements and propose practical solutions. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details