    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Senior-IT-Consultant-%28SAP-SuccessFactors%29/1155-en_GB": {
      "title": "Senior IT Consultant (SAP SuccessFactors) Job Details",
      "description": "Senior IT Consultant (SAP SuccessFactors) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Senior IT Consultant (SAP SuccessFactors) We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Senior IT Consultant (SAP SuccessFactors) Posting Start Date: 17/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Communications & Information Technology Employment Type: Fixed Term This role will provide functional support for SuccessFactors modules. Key Responsibilities Provide functional support for SuccessFactors modules, including Employee Central Core, Benefits, Leave, Timesheet, Payroll, Performance & Goals, Recruiting, Learning, Onboarding and Offboarding. Conduct user requirement analysis for enhancements, analyse business information needs gathered, translate into requirement specifications, and secure user signoffs. Evaluate potential solutions and make recommendations to business users. Assist the configuration of SuccessFactors modules, including Role-Based Permission and provide support during system upgrades and patches. Plan, coordinate, conduct and document end-to-end unit and system integration testing, and support users during User Acceptance Testing (UAT). Monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve system integration issues with related platforms, such as payroll or other systems. Work closely with business users to understand requirements and build good rapport. Collabrate with vendors and team members on application maintenance, testing, supporting application patches and upgrades in accordance with policies and procedures. Participate in project implementation activities where required. Ensure adherence to security policies and best practices regarding system data and user access. Job Requirements Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science or a related discipline. At least 8 years of hands-on experience in SAP SuccessFactors support and configuration, with experience across multiple modules, including Role-Based Permissions, Employee Central Core, Benefits, Leave, Timesheet, Payroll, Performance & Goals, Recruiting, Learning, Onboarding and Offboarding. Strong understanding of SAP or SuccessFactors integration points with other business systems like SAP S/4 Hana, Concur and third-party systems. Experience in system testing, troubleshooting, user training and technical/functional documentation Experience with SAP Analytics Cloud (SAC), Robotic Process Automation (RPA) technologies and data analysis systems would be an added advantage. SuccessFactors certification, such as SAP Certified Application Associate would be an added advantage. Experience in HR technology and processes with a focus on automation, process improvement and efficiency would be an added advantage. Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills to effectively analyze functional requirements and translate them into effective technical solutions. Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot and resolve issues at both the functional and technical levels. Self-motivated and able to work independently, while also being an effective team player and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work collaboratively with cross-functional teams and external stakeholders. Apply Now Job Alerts Link O