    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Fellow-%28Food-Extrusion-Technology%29-VT/1153-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Food Extrusion Technology)",
      "description": "Research Fellow (Food Extrusion Technology) - VT Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Fellow (Food Extrusion Technology) - VT Posting Start Date: 14/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Diagnostics & Therapeutics Employment Type: Fixed Term We are seeking a hands-on Research Fellow with proven extrusion processing experience to lead the development of fortified rice kernels (FRK) and other elderly-friendly, texture-modified foods . The successful candidate will drive formulation and process work from bench to pilot scale, working closely with the DIGNIFIED team to translate research into deployable food products for older adults and dysphagia-friendly nutrition. About the DIGNIFIED programme The DIGNIFIED Programme at SIT conducts translational research into dysphagia, functional foods, and assistive health technologies, with the goal of improving nutrition, safety, and quality of life for elderly and dysphagic populations. The programme brings together food science, engineering, and clinical expertise to develop practical, evidence-based food and technology solutions, including texture-modified and nutritionally fortified foods aligned with the IDDSI (International Dysphagia Diet Standardisation Initiative) framework. Key Responsibilities Lead the design, formulation, and hands-on operation of extrusion equipment (single- and/or twin-screw) to develop fortified rice kernels and other elderly-friendly / texture-modified food products. Develop and optimise extrusion process parameters (e.g., screw speed, temperature profile, moisture content, die design) to achieve target nutritional, textural, and sensory properties. Formulate products incorporating functional ingredients (e.g., proteins, fibres, micronutrients) into rice-based and other staple food matrices, in line with IDDSI texture levels where applicable. Conduct physicochemical, textural (e.g., TPA), and sensory characterisation of prototypes, and evaluate product performance against dysphagia-friendly and nutritional benchmarks. Scale up promising formulations from lab to pilot-scale trials, and troubleshoot processing issues as they arise. Contribute to peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, and the preparation of grant and project funding proposals. Supervise and mentor research assistants, graduate students, and junior researchers involved in extrusion and product development work. Maintain accurate laboratory records and ensure compliance with food safety, quality, and laboratory safety standards. Collaborate with cross-disciplinary colleagues (food scientists, engineers, clinicians) and, where relevant, industry or research partners. Job Requirements P hD in Food Science, Food Technology, Food Engineering, or a related discipline (candidates nearing completion may be considered). Hands-on experience operating extrusion equipment (pilot-scale or industrial single-/twin-screw extruders) for food product development is essential. Demonstrated experience developing fortified or functional food products; experience with rice-based or cereal-based products is a strong advantage. Familiarity with elderly nutrition, dysphagia diets, texture-modified foods, and the IDDSI framework is highly advantageous. Solid grounding in food formulation, process optimisation, and analytical techniques (e.g., texture profile analysis, proximate analysis). Track record of peer-reviewed publications commensurate with a Research Fellow level. Prior experience mentoring research assistants or graduate students is preferred. Strong communication, project management, and cross-functional collaboration skills. Independent, detail-oriented, and comfortable working hands-on in a laboratory / pilot-plant environment. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
