    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Senior-ExecutiveAssistant-Manager%2C-CET-Operations%2C-SITLEARN-%2811-months-contract%29/1128-en_GB": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, CET Operations, SITLEARN (11-months contract) Job Details",
      "description": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, CET Operations, SITLEARN (11-months contract) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, CET Operations, SITLEARN (11-months contract) Posting Start Date: 10/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: SITLEARN Employment Type: Temporary As the lifelong learning division of the Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT), SITLEARN champions stackable and standalone Continuing Education and Training (CET) that empower working adults to upskill and reskill throughout their careers. Developed in close collaboration with industry and professional bodies, our programmes are designed to address evolving workforce needs and support career growth and transition opportunities. In alignment with the next phase of SkillsFuture, which envisions local universities as “Institutes of Continuous Learning”, our division is expanding its suite of CET and SkillsFuture Career Transition Programme (SCTP) offerings. We are seeking a dedicated and service-oriented professional to support the delivery and administration of these programmes and contribute to a seamless learning experience for our learners. If you are passionate about lifelong learning, enjoy coordinating multiple stakeholders, and thrive in a fast-paced environment, we invite you to apply for the position of Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, SITLEARN (CET Operations). Key Responsibilities Programme Administration and Learner Support: Support the end-to-end administration and operations of CET and SkillsFuture Career Transition Programmes (SCTP), including learner registration, attendance tracking, assessment coordination, learner communications, record maintenance, and accurate documentation in compliance with organisational and funding requirements. Programme Logistics and Delivery Coordination: Coordinate programme logistics, including venue bookings, classroom setup, vendor arrangements, and support for courses conducted in face-to-face, online, and hybrid formats to ensure smooth programme delivery. Stakeholder Coordination, Systems and Process Support: Coordinate with internal stakeholders across various functions, manage account setup and account-related enquiries to support billing operations, support process improvement initiatives, and undertake other operational and administrative duties as assigned. Ad-hoc Assignments: Undertake ad-hoc assignments and other duties as assigned to support the operational needs and priorities of SITLEARN. Job Requirements Degree holder, or Diploma holder with at least two years of relevant experience in programme administration, operations, learner support, or related functions. Prior experience in continuing education, training operations, programme coordination, administrative support, or event logistics will be an advantage. Organised, meticulous and comfortable managing records, schedules, logistics and documentation, with attention to accuracy, confidentiality and compliance requirements. Able to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment, while managing multiple priorities and timelines effectively. Service-oriented, responsive and proactive, with strong written and verbal communication skills to engage learners, colleagues and external stakeholders professionally. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel and PowerPoint; familiarity with online learning, webinar or digital collaboration platforms such as Zoom will be an advantage. We offer a hybrid work arrangement that combines remote and in-person work, subject to work exigencies. The successful candidate may be offered an 11-month contract, with the possibility of renewal based on organisational needs and performance. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how