    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Manager-Senior-Manager-%28Facilities-Operations%29%2C-Estates/1152-en_GB": {
      "title": "Manager / Senior Manager (Facilities Operations), Estates Job Details",
      "description": "Manager / Senior Manager (Facilities Operations), Estates Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Manager / Senior Manager (Facilities Operations), Estates Posting Start Date: 09/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Estates Employment Type: Fixed Term The Manager / Senior Manager (Facilities Operations), Estates oversees daily operations and maintenance of the assigned campus zones, including buildings, fit-out and infrastructure projects which will encompass conducting feasibility studies, budgeting, project programming, procurement, regulatory compliance, design review, quality assurance and project delivery. He or she also oversees campus development inspections, building handover processes, and follow-up on defects rectification to ensure operational readiness and compliance with required standards. Key Responsibilities 1. Campus Operations Oversee daily operations which include checking building systems, vendor management, coordination with users, vendor management, inventory control and event management Manage procurement, tenders, contracts, and system maintenance Manages incident response and reporting Conduct inspections to facilitate taking over from Campus Development contractors, inclusive of safety inspections and services audits Follow up on outstanding works, investigate system failure and rectification works 2. Process Improvement Review and update policies, procedures, and emergency response plans Assess current operations strategies and recommend improvements for potential optimization of maintenance costs Explore the use of automation Implement policies and processes related to facilities operations 3.  Stakeholder Management Manage relationships with internal stakeholders and external stakeholders such as consultants, contractors and service providers on campus operations matters Build collaborative relationships amongst the Facilities Management team and vendors Job Requirements Degree in Engineering, Architectural, Building Services, Facilities Management or related discipline At least 5 years of relevant experience in facilities management, building operations and/or maintenance management Candidates with additional professional qualifications or certifications in Fire Safety Management (FSM), Green Mark Manager (GMM), Green Mark Facility Manager (GMFM), Singapore Certified Energy Manager (SCEM), Safety Coordinator/Supervisor/Officer, Licensed Electrical Worker (LEW) - electrician or technician grade, and/or a Master’s degree will have an added advantage Proficiency in MS Office applications Resourceful, self-driven and able to work effectively both independently and within a team environment Good analytical, communication, written and interpersonal skills Demonstrated ability to manage project budget, timeline, and scope of works effectively Adaptable and resilient in managing change and operating in a fast-paced environment with tight timelines WIlling to support after office hours operation works when necessary and required Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Co