    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Manager%2C-Professional-Officers-Division-%28BSHS%29/1085-en_GB": {
      "title": "Manager, Professional Officers Division (BSHS) Job Details",
      "description": "Manager, Professional Officers Division (BSHS) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Manager, Professional Officers Division (BSHS) We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Manager, Professional Officers Division (BSHS) Posting Start Date: 04/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Professional Officers Employment Type: Fixed Term At SIT's Professional Officers Division, we bring our rich industry experience and technical skills into our work, creating a better physical environment where learning and innovation take place. We work with teaching programmes and innovation projects to improve the skills of our students and strengthen and energize our industry and the wider community. We are seeking an experienced Technical Officer (Manager) to oversee our Business, Social & Health Sciences (BSHS) laboratory operations and maintenance, ensuring laboratories remain safe, fully operational, and conducive for teaching, research, and training activities. As the Technical Officer Team Lead, the incumbent will lead a team of Technical Officers and serve as the primary liaison with key stakeholders. Reporting to the Assistant Director (Lab Operations & Sustainability) and working closely with the Team Lead (Lead Professional Officer), BSHS, the successful candidate will be responsible for: Leading and managing daily laboratory operations and maintenance activities. Planning and managing laboratory budgets and resources effectively. Driving continuous improvement initiatives and implementing best practices in laboratory operations and management. Setting performance goals, guiding professional development, and overseeing the deployment of direct reports. Oversee effective deployment of laboratory student committee. The ideal candidate is a strong people leader with proven experience in laboratory management, operational planning and budgetary management, stakeholder engagement, coupled with a commitment to excellence, safety, and continuous improvement. Key Responsibilities: Lab Operations Lead and manage laboratory operations to ensure readiness for teaching and applied research. Responsible for the daily housekeeping and maintenance to ensure safety, cleanliness and tidiness of laboratories. Responsible for the tracking and maintaining of laboratory documentation (e.g. equipment manual, risk assessment, Material Safety Data Sheet, service reports and other safety certificates). Responsible for developing and managing inventory system to ensure availability of consumables in the lab. Manage the process of providing support to students and other lab users’ access to laboratory resources. Responsible for maintaining inventory of laboratory equipment and consumables. Manage the users’ loans and monitor availability of laboratory inventory and consumables. Monitor, collect and analyze data of laboratory utilization. Involved in conducting lab visits and generic lab demonstration. Lab Process Improvements Assist to design and develop the laboratory continuously to ensure industry relevance and co-create an authentic learning environment for students’ learning and applied research endeavours. Lead and drive continuous improvement initiatives to enhance efficiency, utilisation, and user experience. Lab Procurement & Budget Ownership Manage the procurement for laboratory equipment and consumables to ensure readiness of the laboratory for teaching. Manage laboratory budgets, including procurement planning and cost optimisation. Lab Safety & Risk Management Ensure and be responsible for a safe laboratory environment in compliance with safety regulations and standards. Conduct and/or manage routine safety checks and maintain a safe laboratory environment in compliance with safety regulations and standards To de-conflict risks arising from different laboratory users through assessing the approved user risk assessments within teaching labs and making necessary alternative arrangements for users. Team Management Supervise and manage a team of technical officers. Manage TOs’ workload, monitor TOs’ performances, and ensure operational effectiveness. Provide coaching and guidance to develop staff capabilities. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
