    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Manager%2C-Professional-Officers-Division-%28BSHS%29/1146-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Professional Officers Division (BSHS) Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Manager, Professional Officers Division (BSHS) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Assistant Manager, Professional Officers Division (BSHS) Posting Start Date: 04/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Professional Officers Employment Type: Fixed Term At SIT's Professional Officers Division, we bring our rich industry experience and technical skills into our work, creating a better physical environment where learning and innovation take place. We work with teaching programmes and innovation projects to improve the skills of our students and strengthen and energize our industry and the wider community. We are seeking an experienced Technical Officer (Assistant Manager) to oversee our Business, Social & Health Sciences (BSHS) laboratory operations and maintenance, ensuring laboratories remain safe, fully operational, and conducive for teaching, research, and training activities. Reporting to Technical Officer Team Lead (TO TL), BSHS, the successful candidate will be responsible for: Managing daily laboratory operations and maintenance activities. Coordinating and resolving operational issues in the laboratories. Driving continuous improvement initiatives and implementing best practices in laboratory operations and management. Supporting cost-effective procurement for the laboratories. Purchasing and monitoring of consumables usage. The ideal candidate is a people leader with proven experience in laboratory management, operational planning and budgetary management, stakeholder engagement, coupled with a commitment to excellence, safety, and continuous improvement. Key Responsibilities: Lab Operations Execute measures to ensure the readiness of the laboratory to support students and other users in collaboration with fellow colleagues. Perform daily housekeeping and maintenance to ensure safety, cleanliness and tidiness of laboratories. Support teaching staff and Professional Officers in the set-up of experiments, prepare materials or consumables, troubleshoot, operation and maintenance of laboratory equipment and software. Support in tracking and maintaining laboratory documentation (e.g. equipment manual, risk assessment, Material Safety Data Sheet, service reports and other safety certificates). Assist to provide support to students’ access to laboratory resources. Assist to track and manage loan of tools as well as equipment to students and staff. Support in maintaining inventory of laboratory equipment and consumables. Manage the users’ loans and monitor availability of laboratory inventory and consumables. Monitor and collect data of laboratory utilization. Lab Process Improvements Assist to design and develop the laboratory continuously to ensure industry relevance and co-create an authentic learning environment for students’ learning and applied research endeavours. Lab Procurement Support Assist in procurement of laboratory equipment and procure consumables. Lab Safety & Risk Management Support in ensuring compliance with work, safety, and health regulations in the laboratories. Conduct and/or manage routine safety checks and maintain a safe laboratory environment in compliance with safety regulations and standards Ensure compliance with work, safety and health regulations in the laboratories. Ensure adherence to safety procedures and regulatory requirements Assist in preparing safety documentation and audits Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and 