    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Fellow-Research-Engineer-%28AI-and-XR%29-FG/1141-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI and XR)",
      "description": "Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI and XR) - FG Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI and XR) - FG Posting Start Date: 03/09/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: AI & Data Science Employment Type: Fixed Term We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow / Research Engineer to join a research project on the digitalization and intelligence of train operations and maintenance. The project brings together researchers and industry partners to develop and deploy advanced Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Extended Reality (XR) based solutions for real-world railway operations and maintenance. Key Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Work closely with other research team members to research, develop, and integrate AI and XR technologies for railway operations, inspection, maintenance, and training. Participate in system implementation, experimentation, data collection, evaluation, deployment, and field testing in real-world railway environments. Work closely with railway operators, train manufacturers, and other industry stakeholders to understand operational requirements and translate them into practical technical solutions. Prepare technical reports, research papers, project presentations, system documentation, and other project deliverables. Contribute to research publications, demonstrations, intellectual property, and technology translation arising from the project. Requirements Applicants should preferably have: A Doctorate degree for Research Fellow and a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree for Research Engineer in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Software Engineering, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, or a related discipline. Prior training and/or hands-on experience in both AI and XR development. Candidates should be able to demonstrate relevant knowledge or project experience in these two areas. Relevant industry experience, preferably involving the development, integration, deployment, or evaluation of AI, XR, or other intelligent systems in practical applications. Hands-on experience with AI/deep-learning frameworks such as PyTorch and/or TensorFlow. Familiar with Unity or other real-time 3D/XR development platforms, and preferably experience developing applications for AR/VR/MR devices. A good track record in technical communication, including experience in preparing technical reports, research or technical papers, project documentation, and technical presentations. Good communication and teamwork skills, with the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary research team and collaborate with industry partners. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
