    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Engineer-%28in-Creative-Technologist-&-Design%29-JVK/1132-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (in Creative Technologist & Design)",
      "description": "Research Engineer (in Creative Technologist & Design) - JVK Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Engineer (in Creative Technologist & Design) - JVK Posting Start Date: 28/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Business, Communication and Design Employment Type: Fixed Term Overview: The NHB-SIT Joint Lab for Digital Heritage is seeking a Creative Technologist with skills in web development, software prototyping, design research, and digital innovation. The Joint Lab is a collaboration between the National Heritage Board (NHB) and the Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT), established to build foundational digital heritage capabilities through innovation, applied research, and public engagement. Its work supports digital transformation across documentation, preservation, exhibition-making, research, and audience engagement, including emerging formats such as time-based media, born-digital artworks, 3D assets, digital twins, interactive experiences, and digital archives. This role is suited for someone who is proactive, curious, and comfortable working across technology, design, and research. You will collaborate with researchers, heritage professionals, designers, and technical teams to understand user needs, prototype ideas, facilitate design activities, and develop digital tools for heritage research and public engagement. Key Responsibilities: Web Development & Technical Prototyping - Design, develop, and maintain user-friendly web applications, prototypes, and digital tools for heritage research, documentation, interpretation, and public engagement. - Contribute to front-end and basic back-end development, including API integration, data handling, and deployment workflows. - Create proof-of-concept applications and interactive prototypes for digital heritage experiences. - Support projects involving digital archives, 3D assets, multimedia collections, born-digital materials, digital twins, or other emerging digital heritage formats. Design Research & User-Centered Design - Apply design thinking and user-centred design methods to understand project contexts, define user needs, frame problems, generate ideas, and test solutions. - Support design research activities, including stakeholder interviews, user observations, journey mapping, desktop research, usability testing, and synthesis of insights. - Create low- to high-fidelity prototypes, wireframes, and interaction flows to explore and communicate design ideas. - Assist in planning, facilitating, and documenting design workshops, co-creation sessions, stakeholder engagements, and collaborative ideation activities. - Collaborate with researchers, heritage professionals, designers, and technical teams to translate insights and project needs into practical digital solutions. Research Documentation & Knowledge Sharing - Contribute to research documentation and publication outputs, including literature reviews, project reports, case studies, conference submissions, and research papers where relevant. - Document code, design decisions, research insights, workflows, and technical processes to support knowledge transfer and project continuity. Qualifications & Experience: - Degree in data science, AI, database development (especially in the area of human-centred design, UX/Ui, front-end development, game development) - A proactive, self-motivated attitude and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. - Interest in digital heritage, cultural technologies, museums, archives, exhibitions, or public engagement. - Interest or experience in creative coding, interactive installations, digital storytelling, data visualization, 3D web technologies, immersive media, digital preservation, or cultural collections. (Preferred) - Previous personal projects, internships, coursework, or portfolio work in web development, creative technology, design research, interaction design, or interactive media. (Preferred) Web & Software Development - Good knowledge of web development fundamentals, including HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. - Experience or coursework with front-end frameworks such as React, Vue.js, or similar technologies. - Some exposure to back-end development using Node.js, Python, or similar frameworks. - Experience with version control systems such as Git. (Preferred) - Experience working with simple data storage, APIs, or cloud platforms such as Firebase, Supabase, Airtable, Google Sheets APIs, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, or MySQL. (Preferred) - Familiarity with web hosting, deployment environments, cloud platforms, or basic DevOps workflows. (Preferred) Design Research & Prototyping - Interest in design research, design thinking, user-centred design, service design, or interaction design. - Ability to translate user needs, research insights, and stakeholder requirements into practical digital concepts or prototypes. - Willingness to support design workshops, stakeholder sessions, and collaborative research activities. - Experience creating wireframes, prototypes, user flows, design systems, or interface mock-ups using tools such as Figma, Miro, Adobe Creative Suite, or similar platforms. (Preferred) - Exposure to qualitative research methods, usability testing, stakeholder engagement, workshop facilitation, or co-design methods. (Preferred) Research, Writing & Documentation - Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to document processes, summarize insights, and contribute to reports or research outputs. - Experience contributing to research papers, academic writing, project reports, technical documentation, or conference submissions. (Preferred) About the Joint Lab: The NHB–SIT Joint Lab for Digital Heritage is a strategic partnership designed to advance digital transformation through targeted innovation, applied research, design-led experimentation, and public engagement. Its work supports new capabilities for documentation, preservation, exhibition-making, research, and audience engagement. By exploring emerging digital formats, technologies, and human-centred design approaches, the Joint Lab aims to benefit NHB, the wider heritage sector, and adjacent industries through skills development, new technology applications, research dissemination, and community engagement. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
