    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Manager%2C-Admissions-and-Financial-Aid/1133-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Admissions and Financial Aid Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Manager, Admissions and Financial Aid Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Assistant Manager, Admissions and Financial Aid Posting Start Date: 26/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Admissions and Financial Aid Employment Type: Fixed Term The Assistant Manager will support the Admissions and Financial Aid (AFA) Division in attracting and recruiting qualified applicants to the Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT). The role will involve international student recruitment, including developing relationships with key partner schools across Asia, visiting overseas high schools, and representing SIT at education fairs and recruitment activities. Overseas travel is a necessary component of the role. The role will also support undergraduate admissions and financial aid operations, including application processing and verification, shortlisting, and applicant engagement. Key Responsibilities Student Recruitment and Outreach Support major recruitment and engagement events such as SIT Open House, school learning journeys, education fairs and outreach programmes. Plan and execute local and international recruitment and outreach initiatives to support the University's enrolment objectives. Represent SIT at local and international education fairs, school visits, and other recruitment activities. Undertake overseas travel as required to support international student recruitment activities. Marketing and Communications Support the development and implementation of marketing and communications initiatives to attract suitable applicants to SIT. Develop and coordinate admissions and recruitment collaterals, digital content and other communication materials. Work with internal stakeholders and external creative, media and production agencies on marketing campaigns and related projects. Support content development and coordination of photography, video and other creative production where required. Admissions and Financial Aid Support Support the Undergraduate Admissions and Financial Aid teams during the admissions cycle, including application processing and verification, shortlisting and other selection-related activities. Respond to applicant enquiries and provide accurate and timely information on admissions, financial aid and related processes. Support systems, processes and applicant touchpoints to ensure a positive and seamless applicant experience. Stakeholder Management Work closely with SIT faculty and other University divisions to support recruitment and enrolment objectives. Engage external partners, schools, educators and other stakeholders professionally and effectively. Uphold SIT's service standards and represent the University positively across all prospective student and public touchpoints. Other Responsibilities Support other areas of the AFA Division, including admissions operations, recruitment and outreach, financial assistance and scholarships, which are part of the Division’s core functions. Undertake other duties and projects as assigned. Requirements A recognised degree from a good university or Polytechnic Diploma. Preferably 3 to 5 years of relevant work experience in a higher educational environment, with a good understanding of social media marketing trends and Gen-Z target audiences, with direct experience in student recruitment, marketing, events, outreach, communications, education or customer engagement. Experience in project management, and in coordinating production shoots (both photography and videography) and working with creative agencies will be a plus. Strong written and spoken English, with the ability to communicate confidently with different audiences. Comfortable delivering presentations and engaging prospective students, parents, educators and senior school representatives. Good interpersonal and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to work effectively with faculty, colleagues, students and external partners. Strong organisational and project management skills, with good attention to detail. Able to manage multiple projects and priorities in a fast-paced environment and work effectively under tight deadlines. Resourceful, adaptable, and willing to take ownership of assigned projects. A strong team player who is also able to work independently. Willing and able to travel overseas for recruitment and outreach activities. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications; proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud will be an added advantage. Proficiency in additional languages, such as Mandarin or Bahasa Indonesia, would be an advantage. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cook