    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Senior-Assistant-Manager%2C-Resource-Planning-Management/1033-en_GB": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Resource Planning Management Job Details",
      "description": "Senior Assistant Manager, Resource Planning Management Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Senior Assistant Manager, Resource Planning Management Posting Start Date: 26/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Professional Officers Employment Type: Fixed Term At Professional Officers Division (POD), we bring our rich industry experience and technical skills into our work, creating a better physical environment where learning and innovation take place. We work with teaching programmes and innovation projects to improve the skills of our students and strengthen our industry and the wider community. Reporting to the Team Lead of Resource Planning and Management (RPM), the incumbent will: manage asset management operations and serve as System Administrator for asset management systems, ensuring accurate asset records, data integrity, system governance, user support and compliance with institutional policies. ensure day-to-day asset and procurement processes are executed accurately, efficiently and in compliance with policies and operational requirements. drive transformation by reviewing workflows, identifying improvement opportunities, and supporting the use of automation, Artificial Intelligence, RFID and digital solutions to strengthen visibility, productivity, compliance and service delivery across the Division. Key Responsibilities 1.Asset Management and Systems Administration Manage the Division’s asset management processes, including asset lifecycle tracking, data updates, asset verification exercises, transfers and disposals, in collaboration with Lab In-Charges (LICs) and asset custodians. Serve as the system administrator for Asset Management Systems, ensuring effective system administration, governance and compliance with institutional policies. This includes data uploads and updates, administer system configurations, and provide user support, troubleshooting and issue resolution for asset management systems. Monitor system performance and data quality, conduct regular validation and reconciliation exercises, and implement corrective actions to maintain accurate, reliable and auditable records. 2. Process Improvement, Automation, AI Enablement, RFID and Workflow Integration Review existing procurement and asset workflows, identify operational pain points and implement practical process improvements to enhance efficiency, turnaround time and controls. Support the use of automation and Artificial Intelligence, such as analytics, document processing and workflow automation, to help operationalise digital solutions, including dashboards, tracking systems and automated workflows . 3. Provide procurement support and guidance to stakeholders while ensuring compliance with procurement processes. 4. Provide secretariat support for division and committee/workgroup meetings. 5. Undertake any other duties as assigned by the Director, POD and supervising officer for the effective support of division operations and activities. Job Requirements University degree with 8 years' experience, preferably in database system management, procurement, and project management. Proficient in using AI and automation tools to drive process improvements and automate workflow, with strong knowledge in project management practices. Adaptable, with the ability to work both independently and collaboratively as an effective team player to achieve objectives. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with excellent written and verbal abilities. Highly organised and detail-oriented, with a strong focus on accuracy and completeness. Positive attitude, with strong interpersonal and rapport-building skills. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that c