    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/%28IaaS-Centre-for-Smart-Urban-Solutions-&-Security%29-DM/1126-en_GB": {
      "title": "(IaaS Centre for Smart Urban Solutions & Security)",
      "description": "(IaaS Centre for Smart Urban Solutions & Security) - DM Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology (IaaS Centre for Smart Urban Solutions & Security) - DM We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now (IaaS Centre for Smart Urban Solutions & Security) - DM Posting Start Date: 19/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Professional Officers Employment Type: Fixed Term Job Purpose The Business Connector works with industry partners, government agencies, and ecosystem stakeholders to co-create commercially viable smart urban and security solutions. They drive projects that enhance urban resilience, public safety, and operational efficiency, while supporting organisations in adopting advanced technologies. The Business Connector for Smart Urban Solutions & Security plays a pivotal role in advancing applied research and innovation projects such as smart cities, urban mobility, built environment technologies, surveillance and security systems, robotics, IoT/IIoT, AI analytics, cybersecurity, and digital twins. Collaborating closely with faculty, industry partners, public agencies, and students, the role focuses on delivering impactful, scalable, and deployable solutions that address real-world urban and security challenges. Key Responsibilities Lead Generation and Prospecting •    Identify and engage potential clients in sectors such as urban infrastructure, public safety, transportation, utilities, and built environment. Through various channels, including cold calls, networking and digital marketing. •    Develop and execute strategies to grow SIT’s footprint in smart urban and security innovation projects. •    Build strong relationships with industry players, government agencies, and solution providers. •    Identify high-value opportunities and translate industry needs into applied research and innovation projects. •    Identify technical professionals who will work with local enterprises to frame projects, identify capabilities needed from the industry ecosystem, IHLs and centres. •    Involve in industry engagements, help to bring in higher value-added and impactful projects for the centres in SIT, IHLs, Polytechnics and ITE. •    Monitor relevant external grant calls that are suitable for the centre. Market Research and Analysis •    Identify emerging trends in smart city development, urban sustainability, security technologies, and digital infrastructure. •    Position SIT as a strategic partner in addressing national and regional priorities in urban solutions and security. Project Management •    Work with industry partners to scope, frame, and co-develop project proposals aligned with operational needs and research strengths. •    Support Principal Investigators (PIs) in securing funding through grants, tenders, and proposals. •    Oversee project delivery, ensuring alignment with timelines, quality, and expected outcomes. •    Track project progress and provide regular updates to stakeholders. Client and Partners Relationship Management •    Establish and maintain partnerships with government agencies (e.g. urban planning, security agencies), enterprises, IHLs, and ecosystem enablers. •    Build and manage a strong pipeline of projects aligned with SIT’s Smart Urban Solutions & Security pillar. •    Facilitate strategic introductions and collaborations across stakeholders to create mutual value. •    Translate industry engagement into sustained partnerships and repeat projects. Ecosystem Development •    Identify and connect relevant capabilities across SIT, industry partners, and research centres to form integrated solutions. •    Support development of multi-agency and cross-sector collaborations for complex urban and security challenges. Professional Development and Expertise •    Stay updated on advancements in urban technologies, public safety systems, cybersecurity, robotics, AI, and regulatory frameworks. •    Continuously build domain expertise to effectively engage stakeholders and shape high-impact projects. Job Requirements •    A degree in Computer Science, Computer or Software Engineering, Business or a related field. An MBA is preferred but relevant business development experience will suffice. •    At least 5 years of relevant industry experience, with a proven track record in marketing and business development. •    Strong knowledge of digital/AI technologies, resource management, and sustainable business practices. •    Strong analytical, project management, and communication skills. •    Experience in writing project proposals and grants will be an added advantage. •    Extensive experience and knowledge of industry practices to bring industry perspective to SIT. •    Keen interest in innovation projects, with demonstrated ability in proposing company solutions to technical problems. •    Strong interpersonal skills and enjoy working closely with colleagues and potential clients Key Competencies •    Strong knowledge of urban challenges, sustainability, and security considerations in Singapore and the region. •    Excellent interpersonal and communication skills for multi-stakeholder engagement. •    Ability to work across multidisciplinary teams (engineering, IT, urban planning, security). •    Proactive and self-driven with strong ownership of deliverables. •    Strong proposal writing, presentation, and stakeholder management skills. •    Analytical thinking with ability to synthesize complex requirements into actionable plans. •    Project management capability to handle multiple concurrent initiatives. Major Challenges •    Navigating complex, multi-stakeholder environments involving government, industry, and academia. •    Addressing interdisciplinary problems requiring knowledge across urban systems, engineering, and security domains. •    Managing multiple projects and stakeholders with competing priorities and timelines. •    Translating evolving and ambiguous urban/security needs into feasible and fundable innovation projects. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Function