    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Engineer-%28Accelerated-Cleaning-Development-and-Changeover%29-IV2/1125-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (Accelerated Cleaning Development and Changeover)",
      "description": "Research Engineer (Accelerated Cleaning Development and Changeover) - IV2 Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Research Engineer (Accelerated Cleaning Development and Changeover) - IV2 We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Engineer (Accelerated Cleaning Development and Changeover) - IV2 Posting Start Date: 18/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Food, Chemical and Biotechnology Employment Type: Fixed Term As a University of Applied Learning, SIT works closely with industry in our research pursuits. Our research staff will have the opportunity to be equipped with applied research skill sets that are relevant to industry demands while working on research projects in SIT. The successful candidate will contribute to the design, development, fabrication, and validation of an advanced chemical cleaning rig for pharmaceutical and chemical engineering applications. The role focuses on engineering design, fluid dynamics, process calculations, equipment integration, and hands-on experimental validation. Key Responsibilities 1. Participate in the design, development and optimisation of novel cleaning systems and associated equipment for pharmaceutical applications. 2. Perform engineering calculations related to fluid flow, spray cleaning, pressure losses, hydraulic performance, jet impingement, momentum transfer and hydraulic jump (Froude number) analysis. 3. Develop engineering drawings, specifications and fabrication requirements for custom components. 4. Coordinate with vendors, workshops and fabricators for manufacture, procurement and assembly of experimental equipment. 5. Lead technical discussions with project stakeholders regarding system design material and equipment selection. 6. Plan and execute laboratory experiments to evaluate cleaning effectiveness and process performance. 7. Collect, analyse and interpret experimental data and prepare technical reports. 8. Troubleshoot equipment, instrumentation and process issues during experimental campaigns. 9. Coordinate procurement activities and maintain project documentation. 10. Carry out risk assessments and ensure compliance with Work, Safety and Health (WSH) regulations. 11. Contribute to publications, conference presentations and project deliverables. 12. The candidate is to communicate with all relevant internal and external stakeholders as required to meet the project deliverables. 13. Any other adhoc duties assigned by supervisor. Key Requirements •    Bachelor’s degree in Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Pharmaceutical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. •    2 to 5 years of relevant industrial or research experience preferred. •    Demonstrable experience in process equipment design, prototyping, pilot plants, laboratory systems or pharmaceutical cleaning and/or changeover operations is advantageous. •    Strong knowledge of fluid mechanics, transport phenomena, material and chemical compatibility. •    Experience with process calculations and engineering design with applications in pharmaceutical contexts. •    Familiarity with pumps, piping systems, valves, spray nozzles and process instrumentation to build prototypes. •    Experience with CAD software (SolidWorks, Fusion360, AutoCAD or equivalent) •    Experience working with vendors and equipment fabrication. •    Ability to independently conduct laboratory experimentation involving handling of chemicals. •    Experience in Computational Fluid Dynamics is advantageous. Key Competencies •    Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. •    Ability to translate engineering concepts into practical solutions. •    Excellent technical communication and documentation skills. •    Self-motivated and able to work independently. •    Strong organisational and project management abilities. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us 