    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Engineer-%28Robotics%29-KK1/1123-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (Robotics)",
      "description": "Research Engineer (Robotics) - KK1 Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Research Engineer (Robotics) - KK1 We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Engineer (Robotics) - KK1 Posting Start Date: 18/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Innovation Hub Employment Type: Fixed Term As a University of Applied Learning, SIT works closely with industry in our research pursuits.  We are seeking a hands-on Research Engineer to develop, integrate, and deploy a vendor-agnostic robotics connectivity layer that links smart automation systems, sensors, and warehouse management platforms within a live logistics environment. Key Responsibilities Participate in and manage the research project with Principal Investigator (PI), Co-PI and the research team members to ensure all project deliverables are met. Undertake these responsibilities in the project: Design, develop, and integrate the robotics connectivity layer: middleware nodes, protocol interfaces (OPC UA, Modbus, MQTT), and data pipelines between automation systems, embedded devices, and backend systems, using ROS 2. Develop station-level integration across the programme's automation processes — interfacing robots, sensors, PLCs, and vision systems into a common, standards-aligned framework. Build and maintain conformance test tooling to validate that vendor systems and interfaces meet the programme's connectivity specifications. Develop embedded software/firmware for data-capture endpoints and support custom electronics bring-up. Support deployment, commissioning, and site-acceptance testing at the industry partner's facility, including troubleshooting in a live operational environment. Maintain technical documentation, interface specifications, and version-controlled codebases to a standard that supports long-term maintainability and knowledge transfer. Coordinate with technical leads, the industry partner's engineering team, and vendors to keep integration on schedule. Carry out Risk Assessment, and ensure compliance with Work, Safety and Health Regulations. Coordinate procurement and liaison with vendors/suppliers. Work independently, as well as within a team, to ensure proper operation and maintenance of equipment. Job Requirements Degree in Mechatronics, Robotics, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a related field. At least 5 years of relevant experience spanning mechatronics, software development, and project delivery. Strong programming ability in C++ (primary), with working proficiency in Python; comfort with C for embedded work. Hands-on experience with ROS/ROS 2 and robotics middleware concepts. Experience integrating industrial hardware — robots, PLCs, sensors, cameras — and familiarity with industrial communication protocols (OPC UA, Modbus, MQTT, or equivalent). Demonstrated project-management capability: able to plan, track, and deliver technical work independently and coordinate across stakeholders. Practical, systems-level troubleshooting skills across the hardware-software boundary. Key Competencies Familiarity with Open-RMF or robotics interoperability frameworks, and awareness of relevant standards (e.g. TR 130:2025). Embedded development on STM32/ESP32/RP-class microcontrollers; PCB bring-up experience. Experience with containerised deployment (Docker), Linux systems, and networking fundamentals (segmentation, industrial networks). Exposure to computer vision or AI-based inspection systems. Prior experience in logistics, warehouse automation, or manufacturing-line integration. Experience working with or alongside an industry partner in an applied-research or deployment setting. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these