    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Director%2C-Business-Development%2C-SITLEARN/1122-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Business Development, SITLEARN Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Business Development, SITLEARN Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Assistant Director, Business Development, SITLEARN Posting Start Date: 18/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: SITLEARN Employment Type: Permanent Are you passionate about education and dedicated to ensuring the success of continuous education training and learning programmes? The SITLEARN, the Singapore Institute of Technology’s lifelong learning division is seeking a dynamic and organised Assistant Director, Business Development, to join our team. About SITLEARN SITLEARN is the lifelong learning arm of the Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT). Our mission is to empower adult learners with industry-relevant skills and knowledge to thrive in a rapidly evolving world. We offer a diverse portfolio of upskilling programmes designed to support career transitions, deepen professional expertise, and foster continuous growth. Role overview The Assistant Director is responsible for driving sustainable CET revenue growth through strategic account development, expansion of B2B opportunities, cultivation of ecosystem partnerships, and development of workforce transformation solutions. The role leads consultative engagements with employers and partners, identifies emerging workforce needs, shapes learning solutions with internal stakeholders, and converts opportunities into scalable and commercially sustainable outcomes. This is an individual contributor role and the candidate is expected to operate independently and collaborate across functions to achieve the annual goals and targets set. Key Responsibilities Drive revenue growth and pipeline management for CET programmes, with clear visibility of committed revenue, qualified B2B pipeline and future growth opportunities. Negotiate and manage contracts, MOUs, partnership agreements and commercial terms to ensure financial viability, margin protection and compliance. Support strategic projects with financial alignment, including account prioritisation, resource planning, course viability assessments and proposal development. Mount partnerships and programmes that are strategic, sustainable and scalable, including custom programmes, stackable pathways, ATL opportunities and corporate academy initiatives. Lead programme, custom learning and workforce transformation opportunity development in collaboration with internal and external stakeholders. Drive stakeholder engagement across academic faculty, industry partners, employers, government agencies and internal functions. Develop go-to-market strategies and nurture leads to drive conversions. Ensure timely execution of contracting, implementation and cross-functional coordination. Review course quality, employer feedback and market signals to implement continuous improvements with stakeholders. Ensure process excellence, accurate CRM records, data-driven pipeline updates and compliance with partnership obligations. Skills and Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree in a relevant discipline (e.g., Education, Business, Human Resource, or related field). A Master’s degree is advantageous. At least 8 years of relevant experience in CET, programme development, business development, workforce development, partnership management or project management within higher education, professional training or a related sector. Proven track record in strategic account development, stakeholder engagement, partnership management, consultative solutioning and negotiation. Able to understand basic legal terminologies for the purpose of negotiation in the various legal docs such as Non-Disclosure Agreements, Collaboration Agreements, MOU and etc. Strong understanding of Singapore’s CET and SkillsFuture landscape, including funding mechanisms, industry trends and employer workforce transformation needs. Strong communication, presentation, consultative selling and stakeholder influence skills. Proficiency in CRM platforms (e.g., Salesforce, MS Teams), data-driven reporting and use of digital or AI-enabled productivity tools. Process-oriented with attention to detail, compliance, commercial sustainability and cross-functional follow-through. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
