    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-FellowEngineer-%28Inspection-Robot%29-FG/1121-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Fellow/Engineer (Inspection Robot)",
      "description": "Research Fellow/Engineer (Inspection Robot) - FG Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Fellow/Engineer (Inspection Robot) - FG Posting Start Date: 17/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Infocomm Technology Employment Type: Fixed Term Research Fellow / Research Engineer (Inspection Robot) We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow / Research Engineer to join a research project on the digitalization and intelligence of train operations and maintenance . The project aims to develop an intelligent robotic system capable of autonomously conducting comprehensive underframe inspections of trains, reducing reliance on manual inspection while improving inspection efficiency, consistency, safety, and traceability. The successful candidate will conduct the research and development of the autonomous robotic platform and its system integration , working closely with researchers, railway operators, train manufacturers, and industry partners to develop and validate the system in real-world railway depot environments. Key Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Research, design, and develop an autonomous robotic system for train underframe inspection. Develop algorithms for robot localization, navigation, path planning, obstacle avoidance, and autonomous mission execution in complex and constrained railway depot environments. Work with other team members to design robotic software architecture, and integrate cameras, illumination systems, depth sensors, LiDAR, actuators, computing devices, and other inspection hardware onto the robotic platform. Work with other team members to integrate robotic hardware, navigation, perception, AI, and inspection modules into an end-to-end prototype. Conduct laboratory experiments and on-site trials in railway depot environments and evaluate the system in terms of navigation accuracy, inspection coverage, reliability, efficiency, safety, and robustness. Work closely with railway operators and industry partners to translate existing underframe inspection procedures into autonomous robotic workflows. Prepare technical reports, research publications, presentations, demonstrations, and other project deliverables. Requirements Applicants should preferably have: A PhD degree for Research Fellow, or Master's/Bachelor's degree with relevant experience for Research Engineer, in Robotics, Mechatronics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related discipline. Relevant hands-on experience in field robotics , preferably involving industrial inspection, autonomous mobile robots, or other real-world robotic applications. Strong knowledge and hands-on experience in one or more of the areas, including: autonomous mobile robots, ROS/ROS2, SLAM and localization, robot navigation and path planning, robot control, sensor fusion, LiDAR and depth sensing, robot hardware and system integration, good programming skills in C++ and/or Python. Experience with edge computing platforms, cameras, LiDAR, IMUs, or related robotic sensors would be advantageous. Strong problem-solving and experimental skills. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively with academic researchers and industry partners. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo vi