    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Engineer-%28in-the-area-of-Foam-Foods%29-KSL/1119-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (in the area of Foam Foods)",
      "description": "Research Engineer (in the area of Foam Foods) - KSL Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Research Engineer (in the area of Foam Foods) - KSL We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Engineer (in the area of Foam Foods) - KSL Posting Start Date: 14/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Health and Social Sciences Employment Type: Fixed Term As a University of Applied Learning, SIT works closely with industry in its research pursuits. The primary responsibility of this role is to support the delivery of a food research project for people with swallowing difficulties through preparation of study samples, coordination of human participant research, data analysis and preparation of project outputs. Key responsibilities: •    Participate in the execution and coordination of the research project with the Principal Investigator, Co-Investigators, collaborators and student researchers to ensure project deliverables are met. •    Prepare and manage foam food prototypes and comparator samples for laboratory and human participant studies. •    Support ethics submissions, study documentation and regulatory requirements for research involving human participants. •    Coordinate participant recruitment, scheduling and study activities at SIT and collaborating clinical sites. •    Assist with data collection, management and analysis for swallowing, sensory and acceptability studies, including frame-by-frame video analysis where required. •    Prepare project updates, reports, presentations, conference abstracts and manuscripts. •    Support procurement, risk assessment and compliance with research governance, food safety, radiation safety and workplace safety requirements. •    Work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team to support timely completion of the project. Minimum Requirements: •    Bachelor's degree in Speech and Language Therapy, Food Science, Food Technology, Nutrition, Biomedical Science, Life Sciences, or a related discipline. •    Interest in human participant research, healthcare research, food science or related areas. •    Willingness to work with research participants and collaborate with clinical and academic partners. •    Prior experience in research, human participant studies, healthcare, food science, or related project work would be advantageous. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used t