    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Engineer-%28Biomass-Processing-and-Bioprocess-Development%29-LH1/1117-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (Biomass Processing and Bioprocess Development)",
      "description": "Research Engineer (Biomass Processing and Bioprocess Development) - LH1 Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Research Engineer (Biomass Processing and Bioprocess Development) - LH1 We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Engineer (Biomass Processing and Bioprocess Development) - LH1 Posting Start Date: 12/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Food, Chemical and Biotechnology Employment Type: Fixed Term As a University of Applied Learning, Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT) works closely with industry in our research pursuits. Our research staff will have the opportunity to be equipped with applied research skill sets that are relevant to industry demands while working on research projects in SIT. We are seeking a highly motivated and hands-on Research Engineer (Biomass Processing and Bioprocess Development) to support an exciting research programme focused on lignocellulosic biomass processing and sustainable bioprocess development. The successful candidate will work closely with the Principal Investigator (PI) and research team to conduct research spanning feedstock preparation, biomass pretreatment, enzymatic hydrolysis, microbial fermentation, and analytical characterization. The role offers opportunities to contribute to scientific publications, collaborate with academic and industry partners, and develop expertise in biomass conversion and biorefinery technologies. Job Responsibilities The Research Engineer will support the successful delivery of the research programme through the following activities: Design, plan, and execute research experiments under the guidance of the Principal Investigator (PI). Conduct laboratory research activities, including feedstock preparation, biomass pretreatment, enzymatic hydrolysis, and microbial fermentation. Perform sample preparation, HPLC analyses, enzyme activity assays, and other analytical procedures to support project objectives. Assist in the maintenance, calibration, and safe operation of laboratory equipment and analytical instruments. Maintain high-quality experimental records and ensure robust data management, quality control, and research documentation practices. Analyse, interpret, and present experimental results using Excel, Python, MATLAB, or other appropriate scientific computing tools. Contribute to feedstock readiness assessments and the development of evaluation frameworks and decision-support matrices. Contribute to the preparation of technical reports, conference presentations, scientific manuscripts, and project deliverables. Ensure compliance with laboratory safety regulations, standard operating procedures, and good research practices. Provide technical guidance and support to undergraduate students in laboratory techniques, experimental methodologies, and laboratory safety practices. Undertake other research-related duties as assigned by the PI. The candidate is to communicate with all relevant internal and external stakeholders as required to meet the project deliverables. Job Requirements Bachelor's or Master's degree in Chemical Engineering, Bioengineering, Biotechnology, Biochemistry, Food Science, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated hands-on experience in HPLC operation, method execution, instrument maintenance, and troubleshooting, fermentation processes, microbiological techniques, enzyme activity assays, and experimental data analysis using Excel, Python, MATLAB, or equivalent software tools. Proven experience in laboratory research, including accurate record-keeping, data management, and adherence to good laboratory practices. Strong ability to plan, execute, analyse, and troubleshoot experimental studies in a systematic and rigorous manner. Ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively within multidisciplinary research teams. Experience in biomass preparation and processing, lignocellulosic biomass conversion, biomass pretreatment, cellulase assays, bioconversion, biorefinery technologies, or bioeconomy-related research will be an advantage. Experience with biomass pretreatment reactors, scientific writing, publication preparation, or industry-linked research projects will be an advantage. Key Competencies The candidate should demonstrate: Strong passion for sustainable bioprocessing, biomass valorisation, and bioresource utilisation. Strong laboratory, analytical, and problem-solving capabilities with attention to detail. Proficiency in analytical instrumentation and techniques, particularly HPLC. Strong quantitative, data analysis, and research documentation skills. Excellent organisational, communication, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently in a dynamic research environment while collaborating effectively with team members. Commitment to laboratory safety, scientific integrity, and research excellence. Interest in mentoring and supporting undergraduate students in research activities. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
