    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Manager%2C-Programme-Development%2C-SITLEARN/1062-en_GB": {
      "title": "Manager, Programme Development, SITLEARN Job Details",
      "description": "Manager, Programme Development, SITLEARN Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Manager, Programme Development, SITLEARN We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Manager, Programme Development, SITLEARN Posting Start Date: 06/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: SITLEARN Employment Type: Fixed Term Are you passionate about education and dedicated to ensuring the success of continuous education training and learning programmes? The SITLEARN, the Singapore Institute of Technology’s lifelong learning division is seeking a dynamic and organised Manager to join our team. About SITLEARN SITLEARN is the lifelong learning arm of the Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT). Our mission is to empower adult learners with industry-relevant skills and knowledge to thrive in a rapidly evolving world. We offer a diverse portfolio of upskilling programmes designed to support career transitions, deepen professional expertise, and foster continuous growth. Why we are hiring As SITLEARN strengthens its Product / Programme Development function, we are looking for a Manager who can shape and develop market-relevant CET offerings, work across functions, and help grow a high-quality programme portfolio. Role Overview This role will lead the strategy, design and lifecycle management of assigned CET programmes and pathways. You will translate industry and workforce capability needs into compelling learning offerings, partner closely with Business Development and Planning teams, and drive portfolio decisions to build, refresh, scale or retire programmes based on evidence and market relevance. Key Responsibilities •    Lead programme strategy, design and product ownership for assigned CET programmes, including learning outcomes, curriculum structure, delivery model and funding alignment. •    Identify industry capability gaps and translate them into coherent programme concepts, pathways or offerings that address real workforce needs. •    Manage the programme portfolio lifecycle by reviewing programme performance, learner outcomes, market relevance and financial indicators, and recommending programmes to scale, refresh, consolidate or retire. •    Develop and sustain a strong trainer and partner ecosystem, including faculty, associate trainers and training partners, to deliver high-quality learner outcomes. •    Work closely with internal stakeholders across Business Development, Planning, Marketing, Grants and Operations teams to ensure programme quality, launch readiness and ongoing improvement. •    Use learner, client and workplace feedback to strengthen programme impact and continuously improve programme design and delivery. Job Requirements •    Tertiary qualification with at least 6–8 years of relevant experience in programme development, curriculum design, training management, or CET-related roles. •    Experience in adult learning, professional education, workforce development or a related environment will be advantageous. •    Strong grounding in instructional design, adult learning principles and outcome-based education. •    Familiarity with the Singapore CET and SkillsFuture landscape, including funding and compliance considerations. •    Strong stakeholder management and cross-functional collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively with faculty, trainers, partners and internal teams. •    Ability to make data-informed decisions using enrolment, learner feedback and performance metrics. If you are excited about building market-relevant learning products and shaping the future of lifelong learning, we welcome your application. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted