    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Business-Connector-%28ICDIICSS%29-RK/1084-en_GB": {
      "title": "Business Connector (ICDI/ICSS)",
      "description": "Business Connector (ICDI/ICSS) - RK Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Business Connector (ICDI/ICSS) - RK We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Business Connector (ICDI/ICSS) - RK Posting Start Date: 05/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Professional Officers Employment Type: Fixed Term Job Purpose SIT’s Innovation-as-a-Service (IaaS) is an open-innovation platform designed to connect industry players, particularly start-ups and SMEs, with the research and technological capabilities of the Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT), local polytechnics, other IHLS and overseas university partners. IaaS Centre of Digital Innovation focuses on assisting company’s to digitalize their operations or products and implementing AI solutions using ready AI tools to ensure a fast implementation to market. IaaS Centre of Smart Urban Solutions and Security focuses on developing innovative technologies and applied solutions to address challenges in urban living, public safety, and security. The Centre brings together multidisciplinary expertise in areas such as sensing technologies, data analytics, artificial intelligence, and smart systems integration to support industry and government partners in translating research into practical, impactful applications. The business connector works with industry partners to co-create commercially viable solutions and outcomes. They deliver on projects that help the industries and businesses to move up the innovation value chain. They accelerate growth by facilitating strategic introductions and partnerships. The success of these initiatives will bring about deeper collaboration with key industry stakeholders that will translate the industry engagement into more innovation projects with SIT. The business connector will play a pivotal role in advancing Digital Innovation/Smart Urban Solutions applied research projects like Chatbots Digitalization, AI, Data Analytics, Machine learning, LLM, RAG, Dashboards, IoT, IIoT, Cloud computing, building management, cybersecurity and etc. Collaborating closely with faculty, industry partners, researchers, other IHLs and students, the business connector will co-create impactful, practical, and commercially viable solutions that helps in the company digitalisation. Key Responsibilities Lead Generation and Prospecting • Identify and target potential clients through various channels, including cold calls, networking and digital marketing. • Help identify and organize outreach events suitable for the Digital Innovation group. • Relationship cultivator - To identify new business opportunities, building and maintaining relationships with potential clients and driving revenue and projects growth. • Develop and implement a comprehensive business development strategy to drive digital innovation and revenue growth for the client. • Technical professional who will work with local enterprises to frame projects, identify capabilities needed from the industry ecosystem, IHLs and centres. • Involve in industry engagements, help to bring in higher value-added and impactful projects for the centres in SIT, IHLs, Polytechnics and ITE. • Monitor relevant external grant calls that are suitable for the centre. Market Research and Analysis • Identify emerging trends and opportunities in Digitalisation/Smart Urban Solutions to position SIT as a key partner in Digital innovation/Smart Urban Solutions and Security. Project Management • Oversee the planning, execution, and delivery of projects, ensuring timely completion and high-quality outcomes. • Help PI secure funding for research and innovation projects through grant applications and proposals. • Monitor project progress and milestones, providing regular updates to stakeholders. Client and Partners Relationship Management • Foster partnerships with businesses, government agencies, IHLs and other stakeholders to develop impactful projects that enhance Digital Innovation outcomes. • Assist the team to develop and manage a pipeline of potential clients and partners, ensuring consistent progress toward revenue targets. • Connect people who should know each other and create win-win scenarios for both SIT and industry partner. Professional Development and Expertise • Stay updated with developments in digital innovation, AI technologies, Smart Urban Solutions & Security including new technologies, regulations, and industry practices. Job Requirements • A degree in Computer Science, Computer or Software Engineering, Business or a related field. An MBA is preferred but relevant business development experience will suffice. • At least 5 years of relevant industry experience, with a proven track record in marketing and business development. • Strong knowledge of digital/AI technologies, smart urban solutions, resource management and sustainable business practices. • Strong analytical, project management, and communication skills. • Experience in writing project proposals and grants will be an added advantage. • Extensive experience and knowledge of industry practices to bring industry perspective to SIT. • Keen interest in innovation projects, with demonstrated ability in proposing company solutions to technical problems. • Strong interpersonal skills and enjoy working closely with colleagues and potential clients Key Competencies • Strong understanding of the sustainability challenges faced by industries and the market landscape in Singapore and the region. • Strong interpersonal and communication skills to collaborate effectively with industry partners, students, and stakeholders. • Ability to work collaboratively in a cross-functional and multidisciplinary environment. • Proactive approach to continuous learning and professional development in the digital innovation field. • Proficient in technical writing and presentation • Possess good analytical and critical thinking skills • Shows good initiative and takes ownership of work undertaken • Some project management skills, including planning and monitoring of digital innovation projects. *Note : The incumbent will be appointed as Research Engineer/Research Fellow if successful. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
