    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-EngineerAssistant-%28in-Digital-Adult-Learning-Quality-Index%29-AYS/1098-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Engineer/Assistant (in Digital Adult Learning Quality Index)",
      "description": "Research Engineer/Assistant (in Digital Adult Learning Quality Index) - AYS Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Engineer/Assistant (in Digital Adult Learning Quality Index) - AYS Posting Start Date: 04/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Health and Social Sciences Employment Type: Fixed Term Job Purpose As a University of Applied Learning, SIT works closely with industry in our research pursuits. Our research staff will have the opportunity to develop applied research capabilities that are relevant to industry and workforce needs while working on research projects in SIT. The primary responsibility of this role is to support the operational delivery and data management for a national study of digital adult-learning quality and outcomes, including stakeholder and participant coordination, multi-provider data collection, survey and diary administration, data quality assurance and preliminary analysis. Key Responsibilities • Support the Principal Investigator in day-to-day delivery and completion of all project milestones and deliverables. • Coordinate participant recruitment, screening, informed consent, scheduling, communications, reimbursement and retention across pilot and field studies conducted with multiple CET providers. • Set up and administer research instruments and workflows using platforms such as Qualtrics • Support stakeholder workshops, Delphi rounds, telephone interviews and provider engagement, including logistics, materials, note-taking, transcription, documentation and follow-up. • Collect, organise, clean, code, merge and quality-check survey, interview, attendance, LMS/telemetry, implementation, assessment and direct-cost data from multiple sources. • Maintain secure and accurate participant trackers, data dictionaries, audit trails and study documentation; de-identify data and follow approved data-management, IRB and PDPA procedures. • Liaise with participants, course teams, partner institutions, vendors and internal administrative units; support procurement, meeting coordination and project administration. • Work independently and within the project team, assist with supervision of student assistants where relevant, and complete/update project risk assessments in accordance with Work, Safety and Health requirements. Job Requirements • Bachelor’s degree in psychology, education, social or behavioural sciences, statistics/data science, business analytics, human-computer interaction, public policy or a related discipline. A relevant Master’s degree and/or research experience will be advantageous. • Foundational knowledge of quantitative research methods and experience with data collection, data cleaning and research documentation. • Strong organisational skills and the ability to coordinate multiple participants, course schedules, providers and follow-up activities accurately. • Good written and spoken communication and confidence interacting professionally with adult learners and institutional stakeholders. • Experience with Qualtrics, longitudinal survey/diary studies, interviews, LMS/telemetry data, adult learning/CET or mixed-methods research will be advantageous. Key Competencies • Careful, systematic and dependable, with strong attention to detail and commitment to data quality and confidentiality. • Able to organise competing tasks, maintain accurate records and follow through on participant and stakeholder commitments. • Strong analytical and problem-solving skills and willingness to learn new research and digital tools. • Professional, respectful and responsive communication with people within and outside the university. • Self-directed and proactive, while knowing when to escalate issues or seek guidance. • Collaborative, adaptable and comfortable working across office, online and provider-based research settings. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
