    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Deputy-Director%2C-Client-and-Partner-Development/713-en_GB": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Client and Partner Development Job Details",
      "description": "Deputy Director, Client and Partner Development Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Deputy Director, Client and Partner Development Posting Start Date: 04/08/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: SITLEARN Employment Type: Permanent Are you passionate about making a difference in lifelong learning and dedicated to ensuring the value and impact of learning to individuals, organisations and society? SITLEARN, Singapore Institute of Technology’s lifelong learning division is seeking a dynamic, resourceful and results oriented Deputy Director, Client and Partner Development to join our team. The SITLEARN Division caters to working adults who are keen to upgrade their skills and offers multiple pathways for companies to retain their talents and individuals to gain access to higher education learning. Together with the National Centre of Excellence (NACE) for Workplace Learning, the first workplace learning centre set up in an Autonomous University and supported by Skills and Workforce Development Agency (SWDA), we are here to help organisations build workplace competencies. Join us as we strive to shape the future of education and empower individuals to thrive in the workforce. As the Deputy Director, Client and Partner Development, you will play an integral role in the leadership team. Your role is to assist the Head of Division, SITLEARN, in strategic CET growth portfolios and initiatives, building long-term capabilities, implementing action plans to fulfill the mission and vision of the university. As the Deputy Director reporting to the Head of Division, SITLEARN and NACE, your role will encompass: Strategic Growth Leadership : Develop and execute a growth strategy, business plan and grow the portfolios within SITLEARN and NACE@SIT. Profit and Loss Management, New Client Acquisition, Proposal Development and Relationship Building : Lead new client acquisition and new business development efforts leading to new revenue streams and profitability. Creation of compelling proposals, pitches, and foster long-term relationships with clients and partners, showcasing the superior value proposition of SIT's signature programmes. Large Key Accounts Management : Acquire new large key accounts, foster relationships and identify opportunities for collaborative initiatives and tailor-made programmes. Solutioning Portfolio Expansion : Drive the expansion of postgraduate, part-time degrees, executive programmes (in-bound and out-bound), skillsfuture career transition programmes, workplace learning and other new portfolios. Exploring new avenues for impactful solutions, revenue generation and market presence. Cross-functional Collaboration : Collaborate with Programme/Course Directors, external trainers, adjuncts, and internal teams to deliver innovative solutions that meet the evolving needs of clients and partners. Business Model Innovation : Develop and implement win-win business models, leveraging funding opportunities where applicable, to enhance the financial sustainability of initiatives e.g., Mentorship support grants and capability development grants. Client Engagement Management : Lead a team and oversee the client engagement processes and touch points, ensuring a seamless and positive experience for stakeholders. Feedback Management : Manage feedback and debrief sessions with program directors, operations, and admin teams as necessary, ensuring continuous improvement and client satisfaction. Strategic Participation : Actively participate in strategic events, outreach activities, and marketing initiatives to enhance the visibility and reputation of SIT. Adaptability and Project Management : Demonstrate adaptability and effectively manage multiple projects simultaneously within tight timelines. Staff Work : Develop papers and reports for senior management. Skills and Qualifications : Minimum of 10 to 15 years of relevant experience within the CET, postgraduate and/or executive education industry. HR workforce strategy, management consulting and business development skillsets to diagnose workforce challenges and support enterprise solutions. Proven record in leading revenue growth and market expansion both locally and regionally. Proven record in seeding leads, winning deals, and business development within the education sector. Experience in handling large key accounts and cultivating strategic partnerships. Proven competencies in solutioning, curriculum design and development and pitching. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Strong relationship-building skills with both internal and external associate faculty. Sets a personal example, following through on promises and commitments to internal and external stakeholders. Effectively manages time and resources, meet deadlines and flag delays. Driven, passionate and determination to succeed and ensure team success. Sets the highest personal performance and behavioral standards for self. Train, mentor and coach team members to deliver results and nurture customer lifetime value. Accepts personal responsibility to make things happen. Adapts quickly and seize opportunities, even in situations of uncertainty. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
