    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Industry-Engagement-Manager%2C-AI-Training-Programme-DS/1078-en_GB": {
      "title": "Industry Engagement Manager, AI Training Programme",
      "description": "Industry Engagement Manager, AI Training Programme - DS Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Industry Engagement Manager, AI Training Programme - DS We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Industry Engagement Manager, AI Training Programme - DS Posting Start Date: 17/07/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Infocomm Technology Employment Type: Fixed Term Job Purpose The Industry Engagement Manager is responsible for managing and deepening relationships with a portfolio of partner companies for the AI Training Programme. The role ensures the continuity, quality, and value of industry partnerships, acting as the bridge between external partners and internal technical teams. The incumbent will exercise independent judgement in assessing account health, interpreting partner needs, identifying emerging issues, and deciding the appropriate follow-up, routing, or escalation required. The incumbent will also coordinate legal agreements, support marketing and events, and exercise sound judgement in managing partner needs and issues, contributing to the programme’s strategic objectives and reputation. Key Responsibilities Drive the negotiation and renewal of partnership agreements, ensuring timely execution and compliance with financial terms. Monitor and track partnership-related revenue streams and financial obligations as part of contract management. Identify opportunities for partnership expansion that may contribute to programme revenue growth. Manage a portfolio of partner companies, ensuring regular engagement and account health. Coordinate legal documentation and maintain accurate records of agreements and renewals. Act as the technical liaison, ensuring partner needs are clearly communicated and routed to the appropriate internal teams. Support the planning and execution of marketing activities, workshops, and showcase events. Provide regular updates and recommendations to the Programme Leader on partner prioritisation, retention risks, and engagement opportunities. Job Requirements Degree in any discipline. Proven relationship or account management experience, ideally managing multiple stakeholders concurrently. Experience managing ambiguous stakeholder requests, prioritising issues, and escalating matters appropriately in a relationship, account management, customer success, technical coordination, or programme environment. Experience coordinating contracts and liaising with legal teams (prior exposure is an advantage). Experience supporting events or marketing activities. Experience managing or supporting Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes. Prior experience in a client-facing technical role (e.g., solutions, pre-sales, customer success, developer relations, or technical project coordination) is strongly preferred. Ability to understand and summarise business and technical discussions for both non-technical and technical stakeholders. Familiarity with the CET landscape and industry collaboration models is an advantage. *Note : The incumbent will be appointed as Research Engineer/Research Fellow if successful. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
