    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Research-Fellow-Research-Engineer-%28AI-for-Railway-Inspection%29-FG/1070-en_GB": {
      "title": "Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI for Railway Inspection)",
      "description": "Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI for Railway Inspection) - FG Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Research Fellow / Research Engineer (AI for Railway Inspection) - FG Posting Start Date: 16/07/2026 Schemes of Service: Research Division: Infocomm Technology Employment Type: Fixed Term Project Overview We are seeking an outstanding and highly motivated Research Fellow (PhD) or Research Engineer (Master's degree) to join an exciting research project on Artificial Intelligence for intelligent railway inspection and predictive maintenance. The project aims to develop next-generation AI solutions for the automatic inspection of train components with multi-modal sensor data, enabling early detection of defects and supporting safer, more reliable, and more efficient railway operations. The successful candidate will conduct cutting-edge research and develop robust AI models capable of analysing inspection data, identifying defects, and assisting maintenance decision-making. The project is conducted in close collaboration with industry partners and offers the opportunity to work on real-world challenges with significant practical impact. Key Responsibilities The successful candidate will be responsible for: Conducting research and development on AI-based solutions for automated defect inspection and condition assessment of train components by designing and developing deep learning, computer vision, and machine learning algorithms. Collaborating with industry partners to understand operational requirements and developing AI pipelines for analysing visual and sensor data collected during inspection processes. Building, training, validating, and deploying AI models for industrial deployment. Designing experiments and evaluating the performance and robustness of developed algorithms. Preparing technical reports, research publications, presentations, and project deliverables. Assisting in supervising junior researchers and students where appropriate. Job Requirements PhD (for Research Fellow) / Master's degree (for Research Engineer) with expertise in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Computer Vision, Machine Learning, Robotics, or a closely related field. Experience in developing, training, validating and deploying AI models for industrial inspection, predictive maintenance, or asset condition monitoring. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and software development skills. Ability to conduct independent research while working effectively within a multidisciplinary team. Written and verbal communication skills. Key Competencies Proven experience in developing AI solutions for industrial inspection, predictive maintenance, or asset condition monitoring. Hands-on experience in deploying AI systems in industrial environments. Experience with defect detection, anomaly detection, or visual inspection systems. Familiarity with multimodal sensing technologies, including RGB imaging, thermal imaging, 3D vision, or other non-destructive inspection methods. Experience with edge AI, real-time inference, or MLOps for industrial applications. Knowledge of railway systems, transportation engineering, or infrastructure inspection. Experience in collaborating with industry partners and delivering applied research. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimising video performance or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
