    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Faculty-in-Accounting-%28Financial-&-Sustainability-Reporting%29/1072-en_GB": {
      "title": "Faculty in Accounting (Financial & Sustainability Reporting) Job Details",
      "description": "Faculty in Accounting (Financial & Sustainability Reporting) Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology Faculty in Accounting (Financial & Sustainability Reporting) We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Faculty in Accounting (Financial & Sustainability Reporting) Posting Start Date: 07/07/2026 Schemes of Service: Faculty Division: Business, Communication and Design Employment Type: Permanent, Fixed Term The Singapore Institute of Technology (SIT) is Singapore’s first University of Applied Learning, offering industry-relevant degree programmes that prepare its graduates to be work- and future-ready professionals. Its mission is to maximise the potential of its learners and to innovate with industry, through an integrated applied learning and research approach, so as to contribute to the economy and society. The university’s unique pedagogy integrates work and study, embracing authentic learning in a real-world environment through collaborations with key strategic partners. Its focus on applied research with business impact is aimed at helping industry innovate and grow. SIT’s centralised campus within the larger Punggol Digital District features a vibrant learning environment where academia and industry will be tightly integrated with the community. SIT espouses an applied learning approach and offers degrees with a strong focus on science and technology. Our faculty work closely with industry on translational research and innovation, as well as provide consultancy on solutions to industry challenges. This well-established nexus with industry endows our graduates with deep skills and work-ready training experience – attuning them to the needs and demands of the future economy. About the Position SIT invites applications for one (1) faculty position in Accounting at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor . Appointment rank will be commensurate with the candidate's qualifications, professional standing, experience, and achievements in academia, industry, research, and leadership. We seek individuals with expertise in financial accounting and corporate reporting, particularly in emerging areas such as sustainability reporting, carbon accounting, financial instruments, and consolidation accounting. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to high-quality teaching, applied research, industry engagement, and academic leadership, while supporting the University's mission of delivering industry-relevant and practice-oriented education. Key Responsibilities Teaching and Learning The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to curriculum development and teaching in one or more of the following areas, including: Financial Accounting Advanced Financial Reporting Sustainability and ESG Reporting Carbon Accounting and Carbon Disclosure Financial Instruments Accounting Corporate Reporting Consolidation Accounting and Group Financial Statements Accounting Standards and Regulatory Reporting The candidate should be able to deliver engaging and industry-relevant learning experiences that integrate contemporary accounting practices, emerging reporting requirements, and real-world applications. Research and Scholarly Activities The successful candidate will be expected to: Undertake and lead research, scholarly, and/or applied research activities in areas relevant to accounting and corporate reporting. Develop translatable research collaborations with industry, government agencies, and professional bodies. Secure competitive research funding, industry projects, consultancy engagements, or translational research opportunities where appropriate. Disseminate research outcomes through academic publications, industry reports, conferences, professional forums, teaching and thought leadership activities. Candidates with prior experience in applied research, industry-funded projects, consultancy work, or real-world implementation projects are particularly encouraged to apply. Industry Engagement The successful candidate is expected to contribute actively to industry engagement through: Building partnerships with organisations and professional bodies. Supporting work-integrated learning initiatives and student industry projects. Developing executive education, continuing professional development, and consultancy activities. Contributing to the advancement of accounting and sustainability reporting practices within industry. Requirements Academic and Professional Qualifications A postgraduate qualification (Master's degree and/or PhD) in Accounting, Sustainability,  or a related discipline from a reputable university is desirable. Candidates who possess extensive and distinguished industry experience, professional expertise, and a strong record of achievements in relevant domains may also be considered, even if they do not possess a doctoral qualification. Professional qualifications such as CA Singapore, CPA Australia, ACA, ACCA, or equivalent will be advantageous. Teaching Expertise Candidates should demonstrate expertise in one or more of the following areas: Carbon Accounting Sustainability and ESG Reporting Financial Instruments Accounting Consolidation Accounting Financial Reporting and Accounting Standards Corporate Reporting Experience in curriculum development and the delivery of industry-relevant accounting education will be highly regarded. Industry Experience Candidates should ideally possess at least three years of relevant industry experience in one or more of the following areas: Financial reporting and corporate accounting Sustainability reporting and ESG disclosures Carbon accounting and climate-related reporting Financial instruments and treasury accounting Regulatory reporting and compliance Substantial industry leadership experience will be particularly valued for appointments at the Associate Professor and Professor levels. Desired Attributes The ideal candidate will possess: Strong expertise in contemporary accounting and reporting practices. The ability to bridge academic knowledge with industry application. A commitment to developing industry-ready graduates. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder engagement skills. The ability to contribute to multidisciplinary collaborations involving accounting, sustainability, digital transformation, and business innovation. Appointment will be made at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor, depending on the candidate's qualifications, experience, professional standing, and demonstrated achievements. Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. All applications must be submitted electronically via the \"Apply Now\" button below. Apply Now Job Alerts Link Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. R