    "https://careers.singaporetech.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Manager-Senior-Assistant-Manager%2C-Registrar's-Office/856-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Senior Assistant Manager, Registrar's Office Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Manager / Senior Assistant Manager, Registrar's Office Job Details | Singapore Institute of Technology We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Home View All Jobs Sign In / View Profile Search Jobs Job Description Apply Now Assistant Manager / Senior Assistant Manager, Registrar's Office Posting Start Date: 30/06/2026 Schemes of Service: Corporate Division: Registrar's Office Employment Type: Fixed Term The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in managing Convocation-related operations and supporting the division’s administrative functions. This position offers an opportunity to collaborate with multiple stakeholders within and beyond the Registrar’s Office, ensuring the seamless delivery of Convocation ceremonies and associated processes. The role also involves driving process improvements and contributing to operational excellence initiatives. Key Responsibilities: Graduation & Awards Administration Oversee and administer all processes related to graduation, ensuring timeliness and accuracy in updating student data and issuance of graduation documents. Coordinate the end-to-end administration of awards, including managing nominations, selection and award. Continuously review workflows and propose improvements to enhance efficiency and accuracy. Event Planning & Execution Plan, coordinate, and deliver Convocation ceremonies, ensuring an exceptional experience for graduates and guests. Manage procurement, logistics, and vendor relationships to ensure successful event execution within budget and timelines. Stakeholder Engagement Liaise and engage effectively with internal divisions, overseas partner universities, and external vendors to ensure smooth operations. Enquiry Management Manage enquiries received via email and telephone in a prompt and effective manner. Provide accurate advice and resolve issues efficiently to ensure timely resolution and service excellence, escalating complex cases where necessary. Division Administration Assist with the division’s administrative matters, including learning administration. Other Duties Undertake any other responsibilities as assigned. Requirements: A recognised degree in any discipline. At least 3 years of relevant work experience. Strong planning, organisational, and coordination skills, coupled with sound administrative capabilities. Ability to exercise independent judgement with a strong sense of ownership. Mature, meticulous, and possessing a high level of integrity. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage diverse stakeholders effectively. Ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Strong problem-solving and critical thinking abilities. A collaborative team player with a growth mindset and excellent interpersonal skills. IT-savvy and proficient in Microsoft Office applications (Excel, Word, PowerPoint); experience with student information systems and/or event management will be an advantage. Apply Now Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Copyright © 2025 Singapore Institute of Technology. All Rights Reserved. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose 